crates/callisto-model/CHANGELOG.md:37:  Residual instance of the same defect class as the earlier `ReleaseOperationRole` fix (which stopped `Ord` from dropping `attestation_policy`): both hand-written `Ord` impls keyed their `version: Version` field on `version.render()` alone, dropping `version.grammar()`. The identical literal string parses under more than one grammar (`"1.2.3"` is valid both as SemVer and PEP 440), so two otherwise-identical `ReleaseOperationId`/`ArtifactSlotId` values that are `Eq`-distinct only by grammar compared `Ordering::Equal`, violating the invariant `BTreeSet`/`BTreeMap` require: `a.cmp(b) == Equal` iff `a == b`. Both now key the version field on `(grammar, raw)` via a shared `version_ord_key` helper.
